# Server rules

- Routes own HTTP parsing, permission guards, status codes, and `toApi()` serialization.
- Domain modules own orchestration and business rules; data modules own MongoDB access.
- Raw MongoDB writes are allowed only in `apps/server/src/data/`.
- Pass `AuditContext` into state-changing data operations. Audit every real write and skip both write and audit for no-ops.
- Validate request bodies and queries with shared Zod schemas plus `parseOrThrow()`.
- Preserve the error contract `{ code, message?, details? }`; field errors use `validation_error` details.
- Protect planner/admin operations with the existing role guards. A profile header is not authentication.
- Keep config errors value-free because values can contain secrets.
- Cover write routes with integration tests and keep audit/write-route coverage complete.
